data module_storage_host_parse_note: String = "Task 4 (module-identity-storage-binding-design.md Phase 1): the host producer build_module_path_index (src/v1/stage0/src/module_path_index) routes through v1_compiler_parse::parse — the same bootstrap parse path the in-graph oracle uses at the module-name grain — so host rows are ParsedFromSource, not a parallel substring scan. DeclarationScanned was deleted with this repoint: it existed only to record honestly that extract_module_path never parsed; keeping it after the repoint would be a second way to say the same thing (§3). Bootstrap host emission records NO spans -- it emits span_index_empty(), because it allocates no occurrences; full OccurrenceId mint parity with v2.compiler.parse's stamp pipeline is a named follow-on (dissolve-on: v1 bootstrap parse stamps NodeOccurrenceIdentity the way parse_production_prepared does)."

